{
	"name": "Life Potion",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/magic/life/cross-beam-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Anyone using one of your potions can apply it to a weapon or food as a bonus action. Applying a potion to an unwilling target requires you to grapple with, or successfully grab on, your target, but allows you to use an action to force-feed the target on a failed Constitution save.</p><p>When poured into the mouth of a creature who died within the last 50 years, this potion restores the target to life with a number of hit points equal to its character level or challenge rating. This does not restore any missing limbs, and if the creature lacks one or more vital organs they become [[/condition id=doomed]].</p>",
